     "text": "On May eighth, nineteen forty-five, victory in Europe was declared, but half the world was still at war, because Japan refused to yield, bound by a command that saw surrender as complete dishonor. You think atomic bombs instantly ended everything when Hiroshima fell August sixth, and Nagasaki three days later, but inside Tokyo, military leadership still planned to fight to the last man. What shattered them was August ninth, when the Soviet Union launched a massive invasion of Manchuria, wiping out their entire northern force and leaving them completely cornered, so Emperor Hirohito made an unprecedented royal broadcast, ordering his troops to lay down their weapons, ending it all on September second, nineteen forty-five, aboard the USS Missouri."
